<http://ops-sys.local/ontology#note/user-disclosed-2026-10-12-the-founding-anecdote-is-real-and-current-the-user-s> <http://ops-sys.local/ontology#noteType> "correction" <http://ops-sys.local/ontology#graph/ws/energy> .
<http://ops-sys.local/ontology#note/user-disclosed-2026-10-12-the-founding-anecdote-is-real-and-current-the-user-s> <http://ops-sys.local/ontology#noteText> "User disclosed 2026-10-12: the founding anecdote is real and current. The user's friend is successfully selling forecasting/optimisation model development in Portugal now (brief describes residential PV, EV wallboxes, import-vs-export decisions, short-term price forecasts, sold to organisations that control customers). This is direct evidence that Portuguese companies pay for models, overriding the web-research finding that no buyer was visible. Portugal-specific enablers: 99% smart meters with 15-min data, 15-min imbalance settlement since Apr 2025, regulation charges 7.99->13.06 EUR/MWh 2025, solar capture 16 EUR/MWh Mar 2026, ~237k home PV systems, no vertically integrated home-energy giant. Next step: interview the friend (buyer type, money mechanism, contract form/size, first-client path, repeatability)." <http://ops-sys.local/ontology#graph/ws/energy> .
