<http://ops-sys.local/ontology#note/track-pt-es-2026-10-11-portugal-first-market-for-pilots-design-partners-second> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://ops-sys.local/ontology#Note> <http://ops-sys.local/ontology#graph/ws/energy> .
<http://ops-sys.local/ontology#note/track-pt-es-2026-10-11-portugal-first-market-for-pilots-design-partners-second> <http://ops-sys.local/ontology#noteText> "Track PT/ES (2026-10-11): Portugal = first market for pilots/design partners, second for revenue: 99% smart meters (6.4M points) with daily 15-min data and consent-based third-party access, full 15-min MTU chain live (DA from 1 Oct 2025), PT DA 66 EUR/MWh 2025, March-2026 solar capture 16 EUR/MWh with curtailment, regulation charges 13 EUR/MWh, <1 MW aggregation written into MPGGS (Diretiva 9/2025), balancing-enabled renewables+BESS 375->1,250 MW; but ~120 MW BESS, one independent aggregator (Ignis), ~2,020 ACC projects almost all proportional sharing settled by E-REDES, EDP 59% retail, no evidence anyone pays for optimisation (only TotalEnergies->Jungle AI 2024). Spain = Iberian revenue market: 784 zero/negative hours 2024, SRAD 1,148-1,775 MW at 42-65 EUR/MW.h with aggregated consumers via retailer >=1 MW since 2026, RD 88/2026 independent aggregator not yet operable, capacity market Orden TED/966/2026 first auction ~2027, BTM batteries 540 MWh, Bamboo Energy = small-vendor success (SaaS to mid-size retailers, success fee)." <http://ops-sys.local/ontology#graph/ws/energy> .
<http://ops-sys.local/ontology#note/track-pt-es-2026-10-11-portugal-first-market-for-pilots-design-partners-second> <http://ops-sys.local/ontology#noteType> "insight" <http://ops-sys.local/ontology#graph/ws/energy> .
