<http://ops-sys.local/ontology#decision/research.round-1-verdict-start-narrow-and-upstream-wedge-1-germany-quant-sub-supplier-15> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://ops-sys.local/ontology#Decision> <http://ops-sys.local/ontology#graph/ws/energy> .
<http://ops-sys.local/ontology#decision/research.round-1-verdict-start-narrow-and-upstream-wedge-1-germany-quant-sub-supplier-15> <http://ops-sys.local/ontology#name> "Round-1 verdict: start narrow and upstream. Wedge 1 = Germany quant sub-supplier (15-min PV, aFRR-energy, intraday-spread forecasts, co-located PV+BESS dispatch) to BESS optimisers/IPPs (Entrix, Kyon) and mid-sized Direktvermarkter on performance share. Wedge 2 = Iberia 15-min production forecasting and aFRR/mFRR bidding for renewables+storage, Portugal for design partners, Spain for revenue. Alternative = quarter-hourly load forecasting for second-tier BKVs (Syneco/Thuega, Suedweststrom, Trianel). Reject residential VPP, NL household imbalance, V2G, communities as buyers, principal BESS optimisation." <http://ops-sys.local/ontology#graph/ws/energy> .
<http://ops-sys.local/ontology#decision/research.round-1-verdict-start-narrow-and-upstream-wedge-1-germany-quant-sub-supplier-15> <http://ops-sys.local/ontology#rationale> "Synthesis of 10 research notes in reports/European energy flexibility startup wedges.md; W1 scored 72, W2 71, W3 66 of 100." <http://ops-sys.local/ontology#graph/ws/energy> .
<http://ops-sys.local/ontology#decision/research.round-1-verdict-start-narrow-and-upstream-wedge-1-germany-quant-sub-supplier-15> <http://ops-sys.local/ontology#status> "active" <http://ops-sys.local/ontology#graph/ws/energy> .
<http://ops-sys.local/ontology#decision/research.round-1-verdict-start-narrow-and-upstream-wedge-1-germany-quant-sub-supplier-15> <http://ops-sys.local/ontology#createdAt> "2026-10-12T10:53:25Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <http://ops-sys.local/ontology#graph/ws/energy> .
