<http://ops-sys.local/ontology#note/user-correction-2026-10-12-rank-markets-on-business-merit-only-founder-location> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://ops-sys.local/ontology#Note> <http://ops-sys.local/ontology#graph/ws/energy> .
<http://ops-sys.local/ontology#note/user-correction-2026-10-12-rank-markets-on-business-merit-only-founder-location> <http://ops-sys.local/ontology#noteText> "User correction 2026-10-12: rank markets on business merit only; founder location and language are not ranking criteria. Re-ranked for a model vendor selling forecasting/bidding to battery and renewable owners: Spain first (highest per-MW BESS revenue, new rules: capacity market, SRAD, 15-min; thin vendor field; small installed base 193 MW Apr 2026), Poland second (582k EUR/MW/yr Jul 2026, 5.1 GW BESS cleared in capacity market, 11-12 GW by 2030; least researched), Germany third (largest current pool ~2.5-5 GW x 150-200k EUR/MW, but compressing and optimisers build in-house), Italy fourth (money mostly in fixed premiums: MACSE, CER GSE premium; zero price floor), Portugal small (~120 MW BESS) and only useful as part of MIBEL with Spain. Next test: run Experiment 3 on DE, ES and PL prices to compare model uplift per MW." <http://ops-sys.local/ontology#graph/ws/energy> .
<http://ops-sys.local/ontology#note/user-correction-2026-10-12-rank-markets-on-business-merit-only-founder-location> <http://ops-sys.local/ontology#noteType> "correction" <http://ops-sys.local/ontology#graph/ws/energy> .
