<http://ops-sys.local/ontology#note/friend-s-business-clarified-2026-10-12-she-builds-ml-optimisation-in-house-for> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://ops-sys.local/ontology#Note> <http://ops-sys.local/ontology#graph/ws/energy> .
<http://ops-sys.local/ontology#note/friend-s-business-clarified-2026-10-12-she-builds-ml-optimisation-in-house-for> <http://ops-sys.local/ontology#noteText> "Friend's business clarified 2026-10-12: she builds ML optimisation in-house for a Portuguese installer that sells full PV+battery+EV systems plus a retrofit controller ('switch') that dynamically routes power between solar, battery, EV, home, grid import and export; the company has tens of thousands of installed households; no continuous optimiser existed before. Portuguese household spreads (indicative, Jun 2026): import 0.165 EUR/kWh simple; ToU vazio 0.109, fora de vazio 0.199, ponta 0.250; surplus export ~0.04 EUR/kWh average, as low as 0.009 (EDP self-billing case); OMIE minus 0.035-0.039 fixed fee. ToU hour change Jul-Dec 2027. Implication: new top wedge = white-label home-energy optimisation engine sold to Iberian installers/HEMS sellers without ML teams (Spain bigger: 540 MWh home batteries added 2025, PVPC 8.2M hourly-priced households); later aggregate fleets for balancing (PT allows <1 MW aggregation). Key unknown: per-home value of smart control vs inverter default; test by simulation on E-REDES+PVGIS+tariffs." <http://ops-sys.local/ontology#graph/ws/energy> .
<http://ops-sys.local/ontology#note/friend-s-business-clarified-2026-10-12-she-builds-ml-optimisation-in-house-for> <http://ops-sys.local/ontology#noteType> "correction" <http://ops-sys.local/ontology#graph/ws/energy> .
